 twelve points to the right. John Cowan won a contested GOP primary in June and enters the fall with a decisive financial edge, having raised roughly $2.3 million to Chris Harden's $76,000, supplemented by outside spending on his behalf. Prediction markets give Cowan about a 95 percent chance of winning.\n\nThe main wrinkle is a single September poll of likely voters that showed Harden ahead by two points, a result at odds with the district's fundamentals and with market pricing. That survey is the only public polling in the race and carries limited weight. Cowan is expected to win by high single digits, with enough residual uncertainty to keep the race out of the safe column.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1084, "margin": -8.05}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0743, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0742, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1332, "margin": -8.5}]}